# Milestone: M3 (activated v0.14.0-refoundation)
# Covers: a urbi_step whose budget runs out mid-strand comes back RUNNING
#         with that strand still on the run queue, rather than running the
#         program out regardless of what the host asked for.
#
#         Previously a placeholder claiming this needed "test-only
#         host-observation hooks frozen into the v1.0 embedding API".  It
#         does not: `## host: step <budget>` prints the URBI_STEP_* result
#         and `## host: live-work` answers urbi_has_live_work, both already
#         public.  What the fixture did need was work that ARRIVES BETWEEN
#         two steps -- a chunk run through `## host: run` is pumped to
#         completion by urbi_run before any step is taken, so the budget
#         never sees it.  A watcher armed on a slot the host then writes is
#         that work: the drain at the top of the next step spawns the body.
# matrix-row: scheduler-budget

## host: run var x = 0
## host: run var done = 0
## host: run at (x > 0) { var i = 0; while (i < 20000) { i = i + 1 }; done = 1 }
## host: set-global x 1
## host: step 1
## host: run done
## host: live-work
## host: step 1000000
## host: run done
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] set-global: ok
[00000000] step: RUNNING
[00000000] 0
[00000000] live-work: true
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 1
